    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_aa6bd732",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_fresh_prince; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows Meghan Markle petting a small dog while a woman holds it. The text overlay \"the fresh prince\" is a derogatory reference to the 1990s TV show \"The Fresh Prince of Bel-Air,\" which was a sitcom starring Will Smith. The phrase \"fresh prince\" is being used here as a mocking, potentially demeaning label for Meghan Markle, implying she is an outsider or not truly belonging in the royal family. This is a harmful meme because it uses a popular cultural reference in a way that could be seen as condescending or dismissive of Meghan Markle's status and identity. The intent is to mock or belittle her, which can be considered harmful as it may contribute to negative perceptions or reinforce stereotypes about her role or place in society. The meme does not contain overtly abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements, but the use of a derogatory nickname for a public figure can still be harmful by undermining her dignity or perceived legitimacy.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
